#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/chapter.rst:2
msgid "Query and Retrieval of MapServer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/chapter.rst:4
msgid ""
"In this chapter, you will explore the query capabilities of MapServer and"
" familiarize yourself with its Mapfile and template requirements. To gain"
" knowledge of these capabilities, you will build a query application that"
" uses most of the query power of MapServer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/chapter.rst:9
msgid ""
"The following sections describe the concepts necessary to understand the "
"query process that operates on MapServer. Although the detailed usage and"
" syntax are described, the function of this section is mainly as the main"
" component of an overview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/chapter.rst:14
msgid ""
"Map browsing can only rely on MapServer to provide the basic functions of"
" Web mapping services. In addition, MapServer also provides powerful "
"spatial and attribute query functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/chapter.rst:18
msgid ""
"In CGI mode, HTML templates are widely used to build queries and organize"
" the information returned by queries, which usually involves complex "
"interactions with map files, templates, and MapServerCGI programs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:3
msgid "MapServer query mechanism"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:5
msgid "Update: 2022-10-7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:7
msgid ""
"In addition to its rendering capabilities, MapServer also provides "
"powerful query functions, and supports spatial query (location based "
"selection) and attribute query (attribute value based selection). To do "
"this without programming support, MapServer uses templates extensively to"
" build queries and present results. This leads to some complex "
"interactions among MapFile, template and MapServer programs. There are "
"also a lot of different query methods and different ways to use "
"templates. For these reasons, MapServer's query tools are probably the "
"most confusing aspect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:16
msgid ""
"MapServer has powerful and complex query functions, but under CGI mode, "
"it lacks the analysis tools that allow real GIS to provide. This overview"
" describes some query functions of MapServer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:22
msgid "Spatial retrieval concept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:25
msgid ""
"Spatial query is a special kind of query supported by geodatabases and "
"spatial databases. Spatial query queries differ from non-spatial SQL "
"queries in many important ways. The two most important differences are: "
"the use of geometric type data such as points, lines, polygons, and "
"queries involving spatial relationships between geometric types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:32
msgid ""
"The two-dimensional or three-dimensional spatial data is used as the "
"basis of the query, and the query results are represented graphically; "
"the spatial query statement is composed of one or more spatial operation "
"operators, including predicates expressing spatial relationships."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:37
msgid ""
"Spatial query and analysis are at the core of GIS, and most of the daily "
"tasks in GIS projects are related to queries. GIS query types can be "
"divided into the following three types: simple attribute query, query "
"related to spatial location, and joint query related to spatial location "
"and attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:44
msgid "Basic requirements for implementing spatial retrieval in MapServer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:47
msgid ""
"The query template is an HTML fragment that is a suitable HTML interface "
"when placed together by the MapServer CGI program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:51
msgid ""
"The following two variables are user-defined variables. If the tag "
"defined by ``[]`` in square brackets is found, MapServer will pass its "
"value to the HTML template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:56
msgid ""
"The ``map`` and ``layer`` variables are interactive MapServer variables "
"that are required by the map application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb4_using-cgi/sec01_mechanism/section.rst:60
msgid ""
"The variable passed by ``map_web`` will replace the ``TEMPLATE`` "
"parameter in the WEB object of the Mapfile. This variable is different "
"from a user-defined variable."
msgstr ""

